From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mssign32: SignerSign and SignerSignEx sign files (3728)

mssign32: SignerSign and SignerSignEx sign files

Both functions returned E_NOTIMPL. They now sign a file through its
subject interface package (wintrust's PE image and flat-file packages): the
certificate comes from a store or a certificate file, the key from the
certificate's key container or a named one, and the signature (with
Authenticode program-name and statement-type attributes, the certificate
chain per policy) is written into the file. The private key must belong to
the certificate (NTE_BAD_PUBLIC_KEY otherwise). The signature index goes to
pdwIndex. Formats without a package give TRUST_E_SUBJECT_FORM_UNKNOWN;
timestamps and .pvk files are not supported.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mssign32/Makefile.in b/dlls/mssign32/Makefile.in
index fc55d80..0b3ca1a 100644
--- a/dlls/mssign32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/mssign32/Makefile.in
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
